  XP level 30 Magic missile spell beats Grayswandir even against 
silver-hating demons.  

  Add in the ability to get multiple hits per casting (e.g. line 
of monsters or bounces) or the Lawful knight carrying the Magic 
Mirror of Merlin and Grayswandir looks a little...wimpy.  (Even 
one extra hit *doubles* the damage done.)

  Magic missile can also be bounced off of a wall into a corridor
of monsters even if the player doesn't have a straight shot into
the corridor.  (Killed a pet that way once.)  This is very nice
in mazes or even small rooms.  Can't do that with Grayswandir.

  Magic missile is a ranged weapon.  Hitting monsters that can't 
hit you back is almost the *definition* of bliss in Nethack.
You can only throw Grayswandir once.  

  So if you compare the damage-dealt/damage-recieved ratio, there
is no comparison.  You use Magic Missile to kill a line of 
monsters before they can attack you at all, making the ratio 
infinite.  Yes, Grayswandir can windshield a lot of monsters, but
it won't act at a distance and can't give you multiple hits per 
attack.  If a monster is within Grayswandir's reach, you're 
within the monster's reach.



  And magic missile won't damage valuable equipment or 
luck-shattering mirrors, unlike the FooBrands or even the other 
attack spells.  (Even drain life will lower enchantments of 
armor/weapons/rings(?) lying in the way.)




