  It's not just the Hp increase, Pw goes up as well.  And 
since by XP level 15 or so you can probably max out Con & Wis
you'll gain a lot more per XP level than you did earlier.

  More Hp means you *can* take more damage.  More Pw means you 
won't take more damage.  And it's more than just absolute
maximum Pw:  The higher your maximum Mana the faster you 
regenerate Mana.  

  Get your Pw high enough, have the Eye of Aethiopica, get 
Int+Wis above 44, and you regenerate Mana so fast that it
takes near-continuous casting of the spell of Digging/Polymorph 
to deplete it.  

  Remember, if you're at max Pw, you're not regenerating Mana,
and therefore losing forever Pw you could have used to cast 
spells.  So practice spells so you can use all those nice skill 
slots to advance in the various spell schools.


  And once you get to XP level 30, the Hp/Pw increase is "free",
in that your XP level stops increasing, so monster difficulty 
level also stops increasing.

